---
import assets from '../data/assets.json';
import Figure from './Figure.astro';

const {page} = Astro.props;
const asset = (id:string) => (assets as any)[id];
---

<article class="case-study rover-case">
  <header class="case-hero rover-hero">
    <h1>{page.title}</h1>
    <div class="project-meta" aria-label="Project details">
      <span>Payload Team Member</span>
      <span>UBC Unmanned Aircraft Systems</span>
      <span>Sep 2019-May 2021</span>
    </div>
    <p class="case-lede">I designed rover and payload system components in SolidWorks and Onshape, then prepared the CAD for 3D-printed proof-of-concept builds used in prototype testing.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="case-section" id="competition-design-problem">
    <h2>Competition Design Problem</h2>
    <p>For the AUVSI competition, the payload system had to release a rover from at least 30 m. After landing, the rover needed to drive through obstacles and complete the ground course. The payload team had to balance the release mechanism, component packaging, rover function, and aircraft weight.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section" id="my-individual-contribution">
    <h2>My Individual Contribution</h2>
    <p>As a member of the payload sub-team, I focused on the rover and drop mechanism. I:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Created the rover wheel, rover assembly, and a motor envelope model used to check component dimensions and spacing.</li>
      <li>Modeled components for a revised payload winch mechanism within the existing payload architecture.</li>
      <li>Prepared CAD models for 3D printing so the team could compare fit and function and select a suitable rover concept.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section" id="cad-and-prototype-development">
    <h2>CAD and Prototype Development</h2>
    <div class="rover-gallery">
      <Figure asset={asset('A30')} number={1} />
      <Figure asset={asset('A31')} number={2} />
      <Figure asset={asset('A32')} number={3} />
    </div>
    <p>The team incorporated the CAD into 3D-printed proof-of-concept builds for prototype testing and rover design selection.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section" id="result">
    <h2>Result</h2>
    <p>The design process produced a rover concept that could be evaluated within the payload system.</p>
    <article class="single-result-card">
      <strong>50%</strong>
      <h3>Payload system weight reduction</h3>
      <p>I contributed to material and design changes, including repurposing components from earlier concepts, that reduced payload system weight by 50%.</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section" id="what-this-demonstrates">
    <h2>What This Demonstrates</h2>
    <p>SolidWorks and Onshape, component design, packaging, 3D-print preparation, prototype testing, design iteration, and multidisciplinary teamwork</p>
    <p class="sharing-boundary"><strong>Public-sharing boundary:</strong> The images show student-team CAD. I describe only the components and concept work I personally completed or contributed to.</p>
  </section>
</article>
